== P2 Fermat-prime realisation of the parity graph (Lemma 1) ==
   p=17, k=4, g=3: parity graph mod 2^4 == +-sqrt graph on F_p^* under dlog_g: True (32 edges)
      loop at 0 (y=1): True ; loop at -1 (y=g^-1): True
   p=257, k=8, g=3: parity graph mod 2^8 == +-sqrt graph on F_p^* under dlog_g: True (512 edges)
      loop at 0 (y=1): True ; loop at -1 (y=g^-1): True
   p=65537, k=16, g=3: parity graph mod 2^16 == +-sqrt graph on F_p^* under dlog_g: True (131072 edges)
      loop at 0 (y=1): True ; loop at -1 (y=g^-1): True
   hostile control: g=2 mod 17 is not a primitive root -> dlog table fails, as it must
== P3 quadratic characters and the first two bits of v_2(3n+s), odd n < 1048576 ==
   v_2(3n+s) >= 2  <=>  s = chi_{-4}(n): True
   v_2(3n+s) >= 3  <=>  s = chi_{-4}(n) and chi_8(n) = -1: True
   level-2 strategies (sigma(1 mod 4), sigma(3 mod 4)) -> behaviour of odd n < 10^5 (steps <= 3000):
      Collatz   descend-below-start: 49999/49999, cycle minima met: [], no descent within 3000 steps or > 10^30: 0
      chi_{-4}  descend-below-start: 49999/49999, cycle minima met: [], no descent within 3000 steps or > 10^30: 0
      -chi_{-4} descend-below-start: 0/49999, cycle minima met: [], no descent within 3000 steps or > 10^30: 49999
      3n-1      descend-below-start: 49997/49999, cycle minima met: [5, 17], no descent within 3000 steps or > 10^30: 0
