== P5 odd squares in the Syracuse orbit (Lemma 5), odd s <= 2000000 ==
   s with (3s^2+1)/4 a square: [(1, 1), (15, 13), (209, 181), (2911, 2521), (40545, 35113), (564719, 489061)]
   Pell y_j (j odd), x^2-3y^2=1: [1, 15, 209, 2911, 40545, 564719] -> match: True
   length-3 chains (u again a hit): [(1, 1)]
   odd iterate m is a 2-adic square (m = 1 mod 8) iff v_next = 2: True
   odd iterate m is a 3-adic square unit (m = 1 mod 3) iff v_prev even: True
== P6 real Bernstein value R(d) = sum 2^{d_l}/q^{l+1} versus the orbit product (Proposition 6) ==
   3n-1 on positive odd n <= 2000: identity R_L = n(1 - prod_{l<L}(1 - 1/(3 m_l))) exact: True; R_L <= n: True
   orbits entering a cycle: closed-form R(d) == n for 1000 of 1000 (mismatches: [])
   3n+1 on positive odd n <= 2000: identity R_L = n(prod_{l<L}(1 + 1/(3 m_l)) - 1) exact: True
   5n+1, n=37: orbit exceeds 10^400 after 3936 odd steps; c_L = m_L 2^{d_L}/5^L at L=[(10, 37.3527937024), (100, 37.37437384803849), (1000, 37.3743738502072), (3936, 37.3743738502072)] ; sum 1/m_l = 0.050424
   5n+1, n=47: orbit exceeds 10^400 after 3938 odd steps; c_L = m_L 2^{d_L}/5^L at L=[(10, 47.8016438272), (100, 47.839198525375195), (1000, 47.839198528265214), (3938, 47.839198528265214)] ; sum 1/m_l = 0.088649
   5n-1, n=9: orbit exceeds 10^400 after 3910 odd steps; c_L = m_L 2^{d_L}/5^L at L=[(10, 8.5286977536), (100, 8.528366852036006), (1000, 8.528366852034727), (3910, 8.528366852034727)] ; sum 1/m_l = 0.266879
   5n-1, n=11: orbit exceeds 10^400 after 3909 odd steps; c_L = m_L 2^{d_L}/5^L at L=[(10, 10.6606624768), (100, 10.660458565044982), (1000, 10.66045856504341), (3909, 10.66045856504341)] ; sum 1/m_l = 0.155768
   (c_L is monotone: increasing on the plus sheet, decreasing and >= 0 on the minus sheet; a positive limit = full-rate divergence)
